Z||000015||Jake_Dragon||11-06-2001||09:59 PM||||  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pjet.jpg">  <P>Because of the increase in volume at the large end of the cone, cold air would be drawn into the inlet side of the exhaust tip.<BR>I have seen it used in other applications, it you replace the motor in the drawing with a compressor and push compressed air into the cone it will draw fresh air into the cone with it. If you have a compressor try it. The Navy also uses a similar device only with water. Because it draws the surrounding water into the exhaust hose any debris would not have to go through a pump. Prerry Jet or something similar is the name (It’s been a long time sense I was in the service) any way it should work for exhaust I don't know how much benefit it would have.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Jake_Dragon (edited 11-06-2001).]||||reg||1
